#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / Linux Kernel Specification
PACKAGE: linux-kernel
LANGUAGE: C, assembly, configuration/build languages
STATUS: W2/W3
ROLE: Core kernel, hardware, memory, scheduling, networking, storage and security boundary

## PROGRAM
The Linux kernel provides the privileged execution environment and interfaces on which the White Edition userland operates.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream Linux kernel / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: firmware/boot -> kernel -> drivers/subsystems -> system calls -> userland
WHITE_EDITION: configuration, hardening, reproducibility, testing overlay

## SPEC
- record exact upstream version and configuration
- preserve hardware compatibility
- establish reproducible configuration/build information
- introduce hardening one controlled change at a time
- retain known-good fallback configuration/kernel

## QUALITY
TEST: build, boot, storage, network, drivers, suspend/resume where supported, modules, security-policy interoperability, performance, recovery
ECONOMY: image size, modules, boot time, memory, device discovery, CPU

## SOURCE POLICY
Kernel is predominantly C with architecture-specific assembly. No broad C/C++ rewrite. Behavioral source changes are W3 until specifically justified and tested.

## SECURITY
Every material hardening change requires an explicit threat model or security rationale, compatibility analysis, and measurable regression evidence.
